internal/l10n/data
==================

CLDR data for package internal/l10n (dates, times, durations, sizes,
numbers and locale names formatted as CMS formats them).

Generated by tools/l10n/extract.py from Babel 2.12.1, the version CMS pins,
which bundles CLDR 42. Do not edit by hand; regenerate with

    make l10n                              # babel==2.12.1 in python3
    make l10n L10N_PYTHON=/path/to/python  # e.g. the virtualenv of a CMS

The output is committed (it is not part of `make generate`). The same run
rewrites ../testdata/golden.json, Babel's outputs that the Go tests must
reproduce byte for byte.

Files
-----

global.json     the locales Babel has data for, the language, territory,
                script and variant aliases and the likely subtags used to
                resolve a locale code, and the code lists the display names
                of every locale file are aligned with
locales.json    catalog directory (locale/<code>) -> CMS identifier
<code>.json     one per language of the interface: identifier and name,
                medium date/time patterns, month, day and day-period names,
                day-period rules, decimal pattern and symbols, plural rules,
                unit patterns (duration-day/hour/minute/second,
                digital-byte), list patterns and display names

